<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls on Portugal 3-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Portugal 3-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of three-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY:23/MAR/00</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED: 25 BLN ESC	  COUPON: 5.375 PCT</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.26116</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 5.27 PCT  LOWEST: 5.25 PCT</p>
<p>    BIDS: 68.55 BLN ESC     PAYMENT FREQUENCY: annual</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 205.38 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
